  "limitations": [
    "Development runtime on one local machine; this is not verified production capacity or an open-loop arrival-rate test. Original pass, duration, actor and SLO flags are preserved, including failures.",
    "Active-actor coverage is the fraction of nonterminal progress samples at the requested target, not proof of continuous activity. Only the final zero-active shutdown sample is excluded; maximum progress gaps include phase boundaries.",
    "Half-hour values subtract cumulative counters at the nearest sample at or before each boundary. Actual sample times and elapsed durations are reported; the final bucket includes the completion tail. No interval latency percentiles are inferred from cumulative percentiles.",
    "Resource peaks are observed per-PID working/private memory samples inside the full run window, including setup; sparse sampling can miss spikes. Known API PIDs are further bounded by recorded restart lifetimes: original from run start, replacements from their event, and each prior PID strictly before its restart. Samples outside those lifetimes are excluded and counted to avoid stale observations after Windows PID reuse. Other PIDs have only the run-window bound; process-generation identity for them is not independently established. No systemwide or simultaneous aggregate memory peak is claimed.",
    "Generator peakWorkingSetBytes is the OS-reported process-lifetime peak, distinct from the maximum working set actually sampled within the run window. Generator observations may be sparse or absent.",
    "Restart correlation requires the old PID present before the recorded event, absent after, and replacement PID present after. It supports the recorded restart but does not independently prove cause, exact downtime, process ancestry or PID generation; raw log evidence is intentionally not copied.",
    "No pool-wait, query-time, worker backlog, SQL, credentials, raw logs or browser/mobile metrics are included. These missing measurements are not zero."
  ]
